      "content": "While ibuprofen can help with pain and inflammation, taking a higher dose might not be the best approach. Overusing ibuprofen can lead to stomach issues and other side effects. Instead, consider taking a lower dose of ibuprofen (200-400mg) as directed, and complementary anti-inflammatory options like arnica gel or capsaicin cream, which are available over-the-counter and can be more targeted. Consult a pharmacist or online for more specific guidance.",
